From 10cf1a2e0fdcd973bfc3ff7e269e90ab6aec4c33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:33:25 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] FaceUnlock: drop the arm64-only Megvii prebuilts from
 required

  TARGET module FaceUnlock requires non-existent TARGET module:
    libFaceDetectCA
  ... 3 more
  build/make/core/main.mk:506: error: Build failed.

The four Megvii prebuilts declare only android_arm64 srcs, so soong emits
no variant on x86_64 and kati fails the required-deps check at
main.mk:497.

TARGET_FACE_UNLOCK_SUPPORTED cannot reach this. It keeps FaceUnlock out
of PRODUCT_PACKAGES, but frameworks/base/services/core statically
requires vendor.aospa.biometrics.face, whose source lives in this
project. That keeps the namespace in ALL_MODULES, and the check at
main.mk:439 iterates ALL_MODULES, so the deps are validated whether or
not the app is installed.

The four modules stay defined below, just unreferenced. Gating the
services/core dependency on a product variable would be the real fix.
---
 Android.bp | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 82a72ca..f3bed18 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -25,11 +25,10 @@ android_app {
         "vendor.aospa.biometrics.face.impl",
     ],
 
+    // The Megvii prebuilts below are android_arm64 only, and frameworks/base
+    // hardcodes a dependency on this namespace, so kati checks them here on
+    // every arch even when this app is not installed.
     required: [
-        "libFaceDetectCA",
-        "libmegface_faceunlock",
-        "libMegviiUnlock",
-        "libMegviiUnlock-jni-1.2",
         "default_permissions_co.aospa.sense.xml",
         "hiddenapi-whitelist-co.aospa.sense.xml",
         "privapp_whitelist_co.aospa.sense.xml",
-- 
